# Shell Non-Interactive Strategy — Windows / PowerShell 7

OpenCode's shell has no TTY. Any command that waits for input hangs until timeout. Environment variables for CI=true, GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0, GIT_PAGER=cat,npm_config_yes=true are auto-set — do not set them again.

## Banned commands (always hang)

Editors: `vim`, `vi`, `nano`, `emacs`, `notepad`, `code`
Pagers: `less`, `more`, `most`, `pg`, `man`
Interactive git: `git add -p`, `git rebase -i`, `git commit` without `-m`
Bare REPLs: `python`, `node`, `irb`, `ghci`, `node`, `py -3.11` (use `-c` or `-e` flag, or a script file)
Interactive shells: `bash -i`, `zsh -i`

## Non-interactive flags — common cases

NPM: `npm install --yes`, `npm init -y`
Yarn: `yarn install --non-interactive`
Bun: `bun init -y`
APT (WSL): `apt-get install -y pkg`, `apt-get upgrade -y`
PIP: `pip install --no-input pkg`

Git commit: `git commit -m "msg"`
Git merge/pull: add `--no-edit`
Git log/diff: add `--no-pager` or use `-n N` to bound output

rm/cp/mv: use `-f` to force, never `-i`
unzip: `unzip -o file.zip`
ssh: `ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no host`
curl: `curl -fsSL url`
wget: `wget -q url`

Docker: never `-it`. For compose: `docker-compose up -d`

## When no flag exists

Echo pipe: `echo "input" | command`
Last resort: `timeout 30 ./script.sh || echo "Timed out"`

## Rule

If a command might prompt and you cannot find a flag, stop and report — do not run it.
